Reach the fallback for DEC private modes libvterm does not model

set_dec_mode() drops an unrecognised mode with a debug log and returns, so
vterm_screen_set_unrecognised_fallbacks never sees it. As with the
private-leader CSIs in 0001, that makes such modes *unreachable* rather
than merely unhandled: an application cannot implement one itself no
matter what it registers.

DEC 2026 (synchronised output) is the live example -- a terminal cannot
support it on top of libvterm's parser, because the sequence never
arrives.

Applied on top of 0001 at build time (see the top-level Makefile);
upstream is otherwise untouched. Worth sending upstream.

--- a/src/state.c
+++ b/src/state.c
@@ -863,6 +863,17 @@
     break;
 
   default:
+    /* Give the application-level fallback a chance before dropping it.
+     * Modes libvterm does not model are not thereby unimplementable --
+     * DEC 2026 (synchronised output) is a live example -- but without
+     * this they are unreachable, since vterm_screen_set_unrecognised_
+     * fallbacks never sees a CSI ? h/l that got this far. */
+    if(state->fallbacks && state->fallbacks->csi) {
+      long fallback_args[1] = { num };
+      (*state->fallbacks->csi)("?", fallback_args, 1, NULL, val ? 'h' : 'l', state->fbdata);
+      return;
+    }
+
     DEBUG_LOG("libvterm: Unknown DEC mode %d\n", num);
     return;
   }

